  "slug": "untitled-topic-7114",
  "summary": "Seven new reports across five taxa resolve how H3K4, H3K9 and H3K27 methylation are targeted to or shielded from specific loci.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is how histone methylation is directed to, or excluded from, particular loci. For H3K27me3, maternal Foxh1 recruits PRC2/Ezh2 in Xenopus, PRC2 shapes parent-of-origin PHE1 binding at Arabidopsis imprinted genes, and CAF-1 supports PRC2-dependent silencing in Neurospora facultative heterochromatin. In mouse ES cells, H3K4 methylation and DNA methylation cooperatively protect regulatory elements from Polycomb. For H3K4me1, Pol II Ser2P redistribution into gene bodies recruits the FLD-LD demethylase complex to license silencing in Arabidopsis. For H3K9, IDC, STWL and PZG recruit SETDB1 via WDE to phf7 in Drosophila, and EHMT1/2 time cortical neurogenesis through H3K9me2-dependent and -independent mechanisms. The new elements are defined recruiters, licensing steps and protective cooperation at individual loci.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
